## Source audit and change

- Pinned Java Push retry/send-back code calls virtual `Message.getProperties()`
  and passes the returned map to the retry message. Rust previously copied
  property entries only from the base `Message` map.
- Added a nullable `MessageExtSubtype::properties` hook and explicit
  `MessageExt` property views/entry iterators. Custom maps are read as owned
  snapshots; base messages retain their existing live read guards. Retry
  message property copying now iterates the virtual subtype entries.
- The invoked Java custom subtype returns a map with
  `subtype-only=visible`; the direct-consume fixture compares the callback
  value and virtual getter count. Rust matches both. The ProcessQueue
  `MAX_OFFSET` override still yields `msgAccCnt=12`.
- Java's `getProperties()` returns its mutable map reference. The Rust hook
  snapshots it, so map identity and mutation aliasing remain an open semantic
  gap. Updated Phase 6, Phase 10 and Phase 18 records and the release checklist.

